The first-party material in this repository is covered by the MIT license in LICENSE. The material listed below
comes from elsewhere; its own terms, given with each item, apply to it.

1. hol-hearth (https://github.com/BenKnill/hol-hearth, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Ben Knill).
   Some proof files are copies of hol-hearth code (all under proof-tree/tasks/bubble-echo/vortex/proofs/):
   - wasm_call.ml is the project's copy of hol-hearth's wasm/proofs/wasm_call.ml, the one-level call model (wasmc):
     its definitions, theorems and tactics. It defines the same constants and theorems as lines 1-467 of that file
     at hol-hearth 6adb41ce, and its first 423 lines are identical to them.
   - chain_c5p_frames.ml copies, verbatim from hol-hearth 6adb41ce, lines 468-589 of wasm/proofs/wasm_call.ml and
     lines 113-1327 of wasm/proofs/wasm_frames.ml: the nested-call reference model (wasmf, wasmn), its lemmas and
     tactics.
   - chain_c5_tacs.ml, chain_c5_leaves.ml and chain_c5_punct_b.ml copy tactics or proofs from hol-hearth 6adb41ce
     (each says so in its header).
   The base WebAssembly model (wasm/proofs/base.ml, wasm.ml, wasm_tactics.ml, wasm_loader.ml, wasm_bigdecode.ml)
   and the profile recipe profiles/wasm.ml are included, byte for byte as at hol-hearth 6adb41ce, under
   replay/profile-wasm/ for the standalone replay (provenance and hashes: replay/profile-wasm/NOTICE.md and
   SHA256SUMS there). The official C5 part 1 run (hol-hearth 6adb41ce) loaded these same files from a
   hol-hearth installation; each other receipt records the profile revision and tree it used (C1 and C2: 81c0fa6c).

2. s2n-bignum (https://github.com/awslabs/s2n-bignum; Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT-0).
   hol-hearth's WebAssembly model and the code copied from it are written in the style of s2n-bignum's
   machine-code proofs, and some tactics follow s2n-bignum ones (for example WASMC_WHILE_UP_TAC follows
   ENSURES_WHILE_UP_TAC). Any such portion is used under the MIT-0 option. replay/profile-wasm/wasm/proofs/base.ml adapts the load list
   of s2n-bignum's x86/proofs/base.ml. No s2n-bignum source file is included (replay/profile-wasm/ carries its
   LICENSE and NOTICE); the proofs load s2n-bignum's common layer from a checkout.

3. HOL Light (https://github.com/jrh13/hol-light; BSD-style license).
   The proofs are HOL Light scripts and load HOL Light from an installation. No HOL Light file is included.

